// Tips shown during the first night (can be switched off in the menus).
(
    order: "Every evening the ferryman brings up to four crates. Order a few products on the right – you pay from the cash drawer.",
    shelve: "Ghosts can only buy what is on a shelf. Pick a product under \"Put products on shelves\", then click a shelf in the shop.",
    open: "Shelves stocked! Mind the atmosphere: shy ghosts flee bright shops, vain ones want a mirror. When you are ready, open the shop.",
    browse: "Ghosts drift in, browse your shelves and queue at the counter. They grow paler while they wait – don't keep them too long.",
    whisper: "The ghost at the front whispers a hint. Hand over the matching product – or apologise if you don't have it.",
    change: "Compare what was paid with the price, count out the change with the coin buttons and press Hand over. Exact change sends a ghost into the light.",
    double_pay: "This ghost forgot it has already paid. Keep the money – or be honest. Ghosts remember kindness.",
    first_sale: "Well done! Keep serving until dawn. Edwin, an old regular, comes by every night with a special wish.",
    morning: "At dawn you see the night's accounts. Items fade after a few nights on the shelves, so don't overstock. The game saves automatically.",
)
